      "extension_id": "ext-experience-brief-900201-v1",
      "dataset_kind": "controlled_synthetic_extension",
      "question": "Create and save a professional four-slide, six-minute decision briefing using Slidev, with a consistent dark design. This is a controlled synthetic training task: all organizations, methods and measurements below are fictional. Use these complete source notes; no external information is needed. The audience must choose a pilot option. Cover context and evaluation limits, present both methods' final evidence, compare calculated success rates and monthly usage costs, and recommend an option with limitations and next steps. Explain which methods satisfy BOTH constraints. Give success rates rounded to one decimal place and exact monthly query costs; use the final audited counts below. Choose the method with higher observed success rate among those meeting both latency and monthly cost limits. Do not portray small offline trials as established production reliability or present proposed next steps as measured results. Persist the actual presentation in the workspace and identify the saved artifact in the final answer.\n\nPlanned monthly volume: 80000 queries. Monthly query-cost limit: USD 4000. Maximum p95 latency: 200 ms. Only query costs are included; staffing, infrastructure and confidence intervals have not been estimated. Both methods ran on the same fixed hardware and task family, with independent test samples.\nFINAL AUDITED: Kestrel: 171 successful out of 200 trials; p95 140 ms; USD 0.031 per query.\nFINAL AUDITED: Spruce: 184 successful out of 200 trials; p95 270 ms; USD 0.049 per query.\nSuperseded preliminary note: Kestrel had 176/200 successes before duplicate records were removed. This earlier figure is not valid for the decision.",
      "servers": {
        "@sylphlab/pdf-reader-mcp": [
          "read_pdf"
        ],
        "slidev-mcp": [
          "get_slidev_usage",
          "check_environment",
